  "verbalization": "Genistein appears to have a dual mechanism of action involving FaDu, the target of multiple pathways. The first pathway links genistein to SK-MEL-30, which is targeted by 3alpha,7alpha,12alpha-Trihydroxy-5alpha-cholan-24-yl sulfate(1-), and ultimately to FaDu. The second pathway connects genistein to Shiga-like toxin 1 subunit B, which is targeted by prilocaine, also leading to FaDu. This suggests that genistein may act through different molecular mechanisms to target FaDu, potentially through distinct pathways or by influencing the activity of different proteins that ultimately converge on FaDu. The evidence supports the idea that genistein could be a broad-acting agent that influences multiple pathways leading to FaDu, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
